  3. Keep software up-to-date: Regularly update your operating system, applications, and antivirus software to ensure that you have the latest security patches.
  4. Use firewalls: Firewalls can help protect your network from unauthorized access by blocking incoming and outgoing traffic based on predetermined rules.
