  6. Back up your data: Regularly backing up your data can help prevent data loss in case of a cyber attack or other disaster.
  7. Educate yourself and others: Cybersecurity threats are constantly evolving, so it's important to stay informed about the latest threats and best practices for protecting your data.

By following these basic cybersecurity practices, you can help protect your computer systems, networks, and data from unauthorized access and other cyber threats.
