2026-05-21 19:44:47,209 - INFO - Response: Vaccines are crucial for public health because they help protect individuals from infectious diseases and prevent the spread of disease in communities. When enough people are vaccinated, it creates herd immunity, which means that even those who cannot be vaccinated due to age or other factors are protected from the disease.

